[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The row parser reads link-only continuation lines as references and a quoted continuation line as the source wording

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-ROW-SOURCE-LINE
TITLE: The row parser reads link-only continuation lines as references and a quoted continuation line as the source wording
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
In view-check.py's row parser: a continuation line that holds nothing but
inline links is the row's references; a continuation line beginning with
'> ' is the row's source wording; both are split off before the trailing
bracket is read, so a bracket on the source line is the row's bracket. A
legend row accepts a fourth part, the by-line label. The wireline carries
references, source and by-label so the renderer draws them apart.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-ROW-REFERENCE-LINES
  ROLE: Governed_By
